# Mobile iPhone deploy (agent-owned)

When working on the Expo iOS app, **the agent installs and launches it** on the unlocked physical iPhone. Do not ask the user to run `ios:device` / `expo run:ios`.

## Device

- Name: `iPhone` (iPhone 15 Pro)
- UDID: `00008130-001964C814F2001C`
- Core Device id: `3428980A-96B2-5B59-8E31-21BB9B0A8A08`
- Team for automatic signing: `L95JGSJJV3`
- Keep `mobile/ios/BacksterOSv2/BacksterOSv2.entitlements` empty (push entitlement blocks signing)

## Commands

```bash
# Prefer this — sets Tailscale Metro host from mobile/.env
cd mobile && node ./scripts/with-packager-hostname.mjs pnpm exec expo run:ios --device "iPhone"
```

Equivalent: `pnpm --filter @backsteros/mobile ios:device` (same wrapper).

Metro must stay up after install (`macbook.tailc7e057.ts.net:8081`). If the phone cannot tap the server row, it can enter `http://macbook.tailc7e057.ts.net:8081` manually. Phone + Mac need Tailscale (or same LAN).

## When to rebuild vs reload

- JS/TS/TSX-only polish: keep Metro running; Fast Refresh is enough. Re-run `expo run:ios --device "iPhone"` if Metro died or the app is missing.
- Native / prebuild / entitlements / pods: rebuild and reinstall with the command above.

If the phone is locked or the developer tunnel is down, ask the user to unlock it and retry the install yourself.
